# rfc-009-video-recommendation.mdc

## Title
RFC 009 – Video Recommendation & Category Suggestions

## Summary
This RFC defines a system to provide video recommendations based on YouTube API suggestions and category relevance. The goal is to assist Admins and Team Leads when adding new content by suggesting related videos.

---

## Goals
- Suggest related YouTube videos when adding a new category or video
- Enable automatic population of suggested video list via API
- Improve content discovery and save manual search time for content managers

## Use Cases
- Admin creates a new category → sees 5 recommended videos based on category name
- Admin adds a new video → system fetches related YouTube videos via keywords
- Team Lead wants to expand a course → system recommends similar videos

## External API
- **YouTube Data API v3**
- Endpoint: `https://www.googleapis.com/youtube/v3/search`
- Query Parameters: `q`, `maxResults=5`, `type=video`, `key=API_KEY`

## UI Implementation
- "Add Video" modal shows sidebar with 5 suggestions
- "Create Category" modal optionally displays suggested videos (inline or tab)
- Each suggestion includes:
  - Thumbnail
  - Title
  - Channel
  - Add to Library button

## Role Permissions
| Role        | Permissions                    |
|-------------|---------------------------------|
| Admin       | See and select suggested videos |
| Team Lead   | See suggestions only            |
| User        | ❌ No access                    |

## Validation Rules
- Suggestions must be limited to `5` per query
- Only videos with public visibility are accepted
- No duplicates with existing video URLs

